    {
      "id": "claim_3682bb8bd72d486a95134e55f8c79184",
      "statement": "Every job handler is registered in openswe/jobs/kinds.py and imported at startup; handlers route by `kind` to agent_schedule (dashboard recurring), reconcile (stale-run safety), baby_sit (PR watch evaluation), background_tasks (sandbox monitoring), session_cost/agent_cost (deferred cost enrichment), announcements, human_review_deadline, workspace_refresh, and thread_wakeup dispatch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/jobs/kinds.py#L1-L190",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0187fa1f4695e0b31f721f491790375b26c121b9bf759086a1135b107e65f350:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d9afc0d3df954f499b1b1e919b41a09c",
      "statement": "When a job handler raises an error, the job worker retries with exponential back-off (30s * 2^(attempts-1), capped at 1 hour) up to MAX_ATTEMPTS (5); cron jobs skip to their next fire on failure while one-shot jobs give up and finish after exhausting retries.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/jobs/queue.py#L120-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bb4355c2109523e5ca6f5a5b14ae94d39055b84f9df99abf933bb65e3924bd1d:"
